Current implementation source 3b2d97f6cae80bd37a0242b19c0fb37ddd358d86 on origin/main f33168270eb82e823847368bf90465c67bdee48d; branch rook-r5h-idle.
All commits signed by Boxy with the machine key. Own four changed paths byte-equal to tested 4fcd8af09f81667d5100b88ea93065b4a5ed68d7: git diff EXIT 0. Final exact normal CI still follows.

Mechanism:
display_link.rs: wake_action distinguishes data invalidation, active display tick, and stale/empty wake. A tick after pause cannot request a new native frame. Real data mixed with a tick and unknown source IDs remain invalidations.
main.rs: retains dirty-source IDs in delivered Wake, early GPU bootstrap and frame drains; tick-only render uses the existing drawable without calling request_frame. Data consumed by an early native redraw still arms the link before an empty queued Wake is ignored.
stall.rs: fixed 16-source numerical counts (delivered wakes, frame drains, redraw requests, attributed frames), explicit overflow, separate redraw/messages/output pending bits, monotonic observation time and atomic IO snapshots. The settle line includes these plus frame/callback/GPU-completed counts. Source attribution is coalesced and non-additive, not a count of every producer mark.
stall/load.rs: ONE TEST-LITERAL default field, accommodating the extended witness. No production change in that file.
Native::frame was reviewed: assigning the latest paused target does not call a pacer or request work. Its latest-target rule, GPU completion, settle deadline and idle assertions remain unchanged.
Headless keeps its bool poll API; native uses poll_with_wakes. No identity, protocol, provider, capture, replay, checkpoint or visual-paint changes from this feature.

